Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: discard HEVC pictures during STREAMOFF

The delivery worker is cancelled before codec stop. Flushing reference
pictures here can schedule it again while the codec lock and workspace
are being destroyed. STREAMOFF discards pending pictures; normal firmware
EOS still flushes them.

---
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -804,7 +804,8 @@ static int codec_hevc_stop(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&hevc->watchdog);
 	mutex_lock(&hevc->lock);
-	codec_hevc_flush_output(sess);
+	/* STREAMOFF discards pictures; do not requeue work after cancellation. */
+	codec_hevc_forget_frames(hevc);
 
 	if (hevc->workspace_vaddr)
 		dma_free_coherent(core->dev, SIZE_WORKSPACE,
